---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Playgrounds" description="Try an engineering idea, change the inputs, and inspect what happens. Start with SQL running in your browser.">
  <article class="playgrounds">
    <header><p class="eyebrow">Learn by trying</p><h1>Playgrounds</h1>
      <p>A worked example gives you an answer to follow. A playground lets you change the question. Start with a guided lesson, predict a result, then alter the inputs and see what happens.</p>
    </header>
    <section aria-labelledby="sql-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Databases and storage</p><h2 id="sql-title"><a href="/learn/databases/relational/sandbox/">SQL sandbox</a></h2>
      <p>Run PostgreSQL in your browser. Join a shop’s records, test a constraint, keep a purchase together, or investigate how a query does its work. Guided lessons provide the starting data and explain the results; you can edit every statement.</p>
      <p>Your practice database belongs to the tab. Resetting restores its starting point, so you can try a different approach. The lessons explain when an experiment needs a full server or several connections.</p>
      <div class="links"><a href="/learn/databases/relational/sandbox/#lessons">Browse SQL lessons →</a><a href="/learn/databases/relational/sandbox/">Explore freely →</a></div>
      <p class="reading">Start with <a href="/learn/databases/relational/">Relational databases</a> for the ideas behind these experiments, or use the <a href="/learn/databases/relational/practice/">local practice guide</a> to run PostgreSQL on your computer.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  .playgrounds { max-width:52rem; margin:auto; }
  header { max-width:43rem; margin-bottom:3rem; }
  h1 { font-size:clamp(2.3rem,6vw,3.5rem); }
  p { line-height:1.8; }
  section { border-block:1px solid var(--color-rule); padding:1.5rem 0; }
  h2 { margin:.4rem 0 1rem; }
  .links { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.8rem 2rem; margin:1.5rem 0; font-family:var(--font-sans); }
  .reading { font-size:.95rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
</style>
